; What each card is worth at ★0, in brackets beside the numbers its rank has
; grown that into -- "(150) 390" where the card back used to say only "390".
;
; Half of a feature a build can leave out; the other half is the switch,
; base_stats_on_card.jaf beside it, and feature.js in this folder names the
; pair.
;
; The figure is the ＨＰ / ＡＴＫ column of archives/Rance10EX_v1_04/8_カードデータ.x
; times five, five being what CalcTotalHp multiplies by at star 0. So it is a
; real state of the card rather than a coefficient, and at ★0 it equals the live
; number beside it exactly. docs/card-base-stats.md has why that figure rather
; than the column itself.
;
; WHAT THE GAME DOES. Every card's displayed HP and ATK is one formula over
; that column, PlayerCard@CalcTotalHp / @CalcTotalAtk (FUNC 28154 / 28153):
;
;     total = (base + 10 * (starRank - 1)) * (5 + star) * (1 + 0.1 * (count - 1))
;
; star is the *character's* rank, shared by every card of that character;
; starRank is the tier it falls in (1 under ★10, then 20, 40, 80, 160, else 6);
; count is how many copies of the card you hold, capped at 重ね上限 + 1 = 11. The
; multiplier is the same for every card in the game, so the column in the table
; is the whole of what tells two characters apart -- and it is the one number
; the game never shows. docs/card-base-stats.md has the derivation and the
; check against a screenshot.
;
; WHY THIS FUNCTION. CardConstructProcessCacheBackCard@Create is the back
; face's base layer: it blends the frame, the art and the three text lines
; (Element, Belong and the card's name), and hands the finished array to
; m_proc keyed by the card Id. Two things follow.
;
; It already holds a FontProperty -- local 7, `fp` -- and already calls
; ConstructProcess::BlendText through it three times, so the addition needs no
; local this function was not compiled with, which is the one thing a .jam
; cannot arrange. The format string is built on the stack the way the layers
; above build theirs, S_PUSH "(%d)" + S_MOD 2, so it needs no string local
; either.
;
; And the cache key is the card Id, which is exactly what the figure depends
; on -- the ×5 is a constant, so nothing here moves with the rank. So the
; bracket is rendered once per card per session, where the rank, the copy count
; and the two live numbers are in @CreateStatus, which runs on every draw. That
; is also the one wart: g_cardCache is a global, so creating or deleting the
; switch file mid-session leaves any card already drawn showing what it was
; drawn with. Everything else about the switch takes effect at once; this one is
; effectively read at launch.
;
; WHY A .jam. alice-tools' .jaf compiler cannot express any of it. Probed
; against this .ain, it answers:
;
;     card.Hp                            Invalid struct member name: Hp
;     fp.SetSize(20)                     Invalid struct member name: SetSize
;     array<CASConstructionProcess> a;   Unresolved typedef
;     p = ConstructProcess::BlendText()  Invalid type as lvalue: struct
;
; -- properties, struct methods, and arrays of struct are all out of reach, and
; they are the whole of what drawing a line on this card is. So the body below
; is FUNC 23037 verbatim, from
;   alice ain dump -c game/ain/Rance10.v1.04.ain
; with the tail added, and CALLFUNC resolves BaseStatsOnCardEnabled by name --
; which means alice-tools has to be handed the .jaf *first*, the order
; feature.js lists them in. Regenerate the body the same way if the game
; version changes: every number here is an index into one build of one .ain.
;
; WHERE THE TEXT GOES. The card is 208x312 -- ConstructProcess::CreateBase says
; so -- and the overlay CG シス／カード／詳細 draws the two labels at x 16..44,
; with the rows banded y 112..138 and y 138..165. @CreateStatus right-aligns
; the live numbers at x=196. So the brackets are left-aligned at x=48, centred
; on each band at y=125 and y=151 (origin 4: left, middle), which leaves the
; live number the whole of the rest of the row to grow leftwards into. At font
; size 20 the widest bracketed figure anything reaches, "(15000)" -- ＡＬＩＣＥ and
; ネプラカス are the only cards over 2000 in a column -- is about 103px against
; the 148 between the label and x=196, so it meets the live number only where
; that number is six digits, which on those cards means a rank in the hundreds.
;
; The origin argument is a numpad: 1,4,7 left / 2,5,8 centre / 3,6,9 right for
; x, and 1,2,3 bottom / 4,5,6 middle / 7,8,9 top for y. It reads backwards from
; the two switch tables in ConstructProcess::BlendText (FUNC 23076), which
; adjust local 3 -- y -- first and local 2 -- x -- second.
;
; Only this face changes. The front of the card and the 統合部隊DATA face are
; CardConstructProcessCacheFront and CardConstructProcessCacheBackCardListInfo,
; separate classes with caches of their own, and neither shows HP or ATK at all.
;
; Item cards go through here too, and most of them carry 0 in both columns --
; so an item reads "(0) 0", which is what it already read minus the brackets.
; No branch for it: the live number is drawn unconditionally by the game
; itself, and matching that is cheaper than a special case.
;
; Save this file as UTF-8 with no BOM. The assembler reads a byte order mark as
; an instruction and stops on line 1 -- "Invalid instruction: ϻ" -- and an
; editor that defaults .jam to UTF-8-with-BOM will quietly put one back.
FUNC 23037
	.LOCALREF proc
	CALLHLL Array Free 13
	.LOCALREF orgName
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28097
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC getOrganizationNameFromId
	S_ASSIGN
	DELETE
	.LOCALREF proc
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::CreateBase
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28121
	CALLMETHOD 0
	IFNZ 0x357b68
	JUMP 0x357d1c
0x357b68:
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／下地／%s所属／アイテム"
	.LOCALREF orgName
	A_REF
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCgMaxAlpha
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF cgName
	S_PUSH "カード／アイテム／"
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28105
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC AlternativeImage::GetCg
	S_ASSIGN
	DELETE
	.LOCALREF proc
	.LOCALREF cgName
	A_REF
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCg
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／枠／%s所属／アイテム"
	.LOCALREF orgName
	A_REF
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCgMaxAlpha
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／詳細"
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCgMaxAlpha
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／属性／下地／%s所属"
	.LOCALREF orgName
	A_REF
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCgMaxAlpha
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／属性／%s"
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28099
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC getElementNameFromId
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 9
	PUSH 9
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCgMaxAlpha
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	JUMP 0x357e6e
0x357d1c:
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／下地／%s所属"
	.LOCALREF orgName
	A_REF
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCg
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "カード／%s"
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28105
	CALLMETHOD 0
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCg
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／詳細"
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCg
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／属性／下地／%s所属"
	.LOCALREF orgName
	A_REF
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 0
	PUSH 0
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCg
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "シス／カード／属性／%s"
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28099
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC getElementNameFromId
	S_MOD 4
	PUSH 9
	PUSH 9
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendCg
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
0x357e6e:
	.LOCALASSIGN r 0
	.LOCALASSIGN g 0
	.LOCALASSIGN b 0
	.LOCALCREATE fp FontProperty
	.LOCALREF fp
	PUSH 29387
	PUSH 25
	CALLMETHOD 1
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : FontProperty@SetSizeの戻り値>"
	POP
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetSizeの戻り値>"
	PUSHLOCALPAGE
	PUSH 4
	PUSHLOCALPAGE
	PUSH 5
	PUSHLOCALPAGE
	PUSH 6
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28099
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC getElementColor
	.LOCALREF fp
	PUSH 29393
	.LOCALREF r
	.LOCALREF g
	.LOCALREF b
	CALLMETHOD 3
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>"
	POP
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>"
	.LOCALREF proc
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28099
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC getElementNameFromId
	.LOCALREF fp
	A_REF
	PUSH 84
	PUSH 41
	PUSH 5
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendText
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	PUSHLOCALPAGE
	PUSH 4
	PUSHLOCALPAGE
	PUSH 5
	PUSHLOCALPAGE
	PUSH 6
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28097
	CALLMETHOD 0
	CALLFUNC getOrganizationColor
	.LOCALREF fp
	PUSH 29393
	.LOCALREF r
	.LOCALREF g
	.LOCALREF b
	CALLMETHOD 3
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#1"
	POP
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#1"
	.LOCALREF proc
	.LOCALREF orgName
	A_REF
	.LOCALREF fp
	A_REF
	PUSH 198
	PUSH 86
	PUSH 9
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendText
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF fp
	PUSH 29393
	PUSH 255
	PUSH 255
	PUSH 255
	CALLMETHOD 3
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#2"
	POP
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#2"
	.LOCALREF proc
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28089
	CALLMETHOD 0
	.LOCALREF fp
	A_REF
	PUSH 105
	PUSH 289
	PUSH 5
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendText
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
; --- added: the two bracketed figures --------------------------------------
;
;   CALLFUNC BaseStatsOnCardEnabled   is the switch file there
;   IFZ skip_base_stats               no: leave the card as the game draws it
;   fp.SetSize(20)                    smaller than the 25 the labels above use
;   fp.SetColorBody(130, 200, 235)    and a colour no live number is drawn in
;   proc.PushBack(BlendText("(%d)" % (card.Hp  * 5), fp, 48, 125, 4))
;   proc.PushBack(BlendText("(%d)" % (card.Atk * 5), fp, 48, 151, 4))
;
; PlayerCard@Hp::get is FUNC 28091 and @Atk::get is 28093 -- the raw column,
; before CalcTotalHp does anything to it. Their #1 twins (28092 / 28094) are the
; compiler's rvalue copies and are not what CalcTotalHp itself calls.
;
; The five is CalcTotalHp's own multiplier at star 0: (5 + star) is 5 there, and
; the tier bonus is 0 with it, so base * 5 is exactly what the card shows at ★0.
; Which is the point of multiplying at all. The bare column is a coefficient --
; a number the game displays nowhere, at no rank -- and a bracket holding one
; has to be explained before it means anything. base * 5 is a state the card
; really passes through, so at ★0 the row reads "(150) 150" and says what the
; bracket is without being told. It costs one digit and reorders nothing: five
; is a constant, so which card is worth more is the same question either way.
;
; The two SetSize / SetColorBody dummies are locals 8 and 11, which the function
; above has already assigned and deleted, so reusing them by name costs nothing
; and adds no slot. Nothing after this point reads fp, so leaving it at size 20
; and blue is safe -- the card's own name was blended white at 25 above.
	CALLFUNC BaseStatsOnCardEnabled
	IFZ skip_base_stats
	.LOCALREF fp
	PUSH 29387
	PUSH 20
	CALLMETHOD 1
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : FontProperty@SetSizeの戻り値>"
	POP
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetSizeの戻り値>"
	.LOCALREF fp
	PUSH 29393
	PUSH 130
	PUSH 200
	PUSH 235
	CALLMETHOD 3
	.STACK_LOCALASSIGN "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#2"
	POP
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#2"
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "(%d)"
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28091
	CALLMETHOD 0
	PUSH 5
	MUL
	S_MOD 2
	.LOCALREF fp
	A_REF
	PUSH 48
	PUSH 125
	PUSH 4
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendText
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
	.LOCALREF proc
	S_PUSH "(%d)"
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28093
	CALLMETHOD 0
	PUSH 5
	MUL
	S_MOD 2
	.LOCALREF fp
	A_REF
	PUSH 48
	PUSH 151
	PUSH 4
	CALLFUNC ConstructProcess::BlendText
	CALLHLL Array PushBack 13
skip_base_stats:
; --- end of the addition ---------------------------------------------------
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#2"
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>#1"
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetColorBodyの戻り値>"
	.LOCALDELETE "<dummy : FontProperty@SetSizeの戻り値>"
	.LOCALDELETE fp
	.STRUCTREF CardConstructProcessCacheBackCard m_proc
	PUSH 35893
	.LOCALREF card
	PUSH 28086
	CALLMETHOD 0
	.LOCALREF proc
	A_REF
	CALLMETHOD 2
	RETURN
ENDFUNC CardConstructProcessCacheBackCard@Create
